<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tarquinius-superbus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tarquinius-superbus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-1">1 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Publius Valerius celebrates a triumph after the Battle of Silva Arsia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In what is traditionally the first year of the Republic, the consul Valerius brought the spoils of the battle against the deposed king Tarquin back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and held a triumph. His four-horse <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> became the usual vehicle of a victorious Roman general.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarquinius-superbus">Tarquin</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-triumph">triumph</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-13">13 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Temple of Jupiter on the Capitoline Hill is dedicated</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-of-jupiter-optimus-maximus">Temple of Jupiter Optimus Maximus</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill">Capitoline Hill</a> was dedicated on the Ides of September in the Republic's first year, by the consul Marcus Horatius Pulvillus. Dionysius of Halicarnassus dated the consecration to 507 BCE.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill">Capitoline Hill</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
