<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/roman-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Roman%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Roman Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Traditional expulsion of Tarquinius Superbus and election of the first consuls</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/aristocracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Aristocracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Aristocracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">By Roman tradition the last king is expelled, and patrician families rule through the Senate and two annual consuls</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">By Roman tradition the last king, Tarquinius Superbus, is expelled and the first two consuls are elected</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/roman-religion"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Roman%20religion.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Roman religion</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The expulsion of Tarquinius Superbus ends Roman kingship and begins the Republic, whose elected magistrates also serve as priests</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/rome"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rome.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rome</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Expulsion of the last king and start of the Republic, by tradition</span></li></ul></section>
